version: "2.0"
description: >-
  packages/gnomon-mods - the first-party Gnomon mods (spec §12.1). They run on
  the same mod-abi:v1 and the same `mod` sandbox profile as any other mod;
  first-party is a trust tier derived from the packageHash pinned in the
  kernel's FIRST_PARTY_PACKAGE_HASHES (packages/gnomon/src/kernel/manifest/install.ts),
  never a wider ABI. Files are LF-pinned (.gitattributes) so the hash is the
  same on every OS.

components:
  workshop-mod:
    description: >-
      #workshop-mod (spec §11.6, G-WSP-01; §19.1 M1.11 slice 3) -
      packages/gnomon-mods/workshop: one view `workshop.strip` (slot sidebar,
      append) with two zones, needs you (one cap per pending card, labelled
      by the card kind) and working (one cap per session: hat = work type,
      filled = Claude, outlined = local, tone hue-<0..7> = project, violet
      only for a KNOT; bob while turn.partial streams, still otherwise,
      `working` text pose under reduced motion). model.mjs is a pure reducer
      + render (sessions and cards bounded at 256 each); index.mjs speaks
      mod-abi:v1 directly (no SDK import, so the pinned packageHash never
      depends on an SDK build) and echoes MOD_ABI_ID. State comes ONLY from
      the host's projected kernel-event feed (#mod-host feed.ts, granted by
      the log.read capability); a host-initiated fixture render may replay
      input.fixtureEvents, a relayed render never can. Declared effects:
      none beyond idle read; tier first-party; installs with
      `gnomon mod install packages/gnomon-mods/workshop` + the root-key card.
      Fixtures strip.json / strip-reduced.json with golden renders
      (test/workshop-mod.test.ts, every OS).
    tags: [mods, first-party, M1.11]
    oracles: [G-WSP-01]

  ledger-mod:
    description: >-
      #ledger-mod - packages/gnomon-mods/ledger, the context and budget
      meter (mod #1 of the mods arc). Two views: `ledger.strip` (slot
      composer.footer, append) - one line for the focused session (relay
      input {hsid}, display only) or all sessions, `182k in · 9k out · 71%
      cache · $0.42 · ⇣ 2 compactions (190k → 41k)` (in = fresh + cache
      reads + cache writes; cache = the share read from cache; a local
      session shows its token total), the budget meter (the over-permit row
      `n of m`, else the highest budget.ladder rung `n of 100%`) and the
      alarms (breaker open, permit denied); `ledger.sheet` (slot sidebar,
      append) - a Table row per session plus the total, meter and alarms.
      Tones: quiet; warn (amber) at a rung >= 75% or an over-permit row;
      deny (vermilion) on a breaker or a denied permit; hue-<0..7> ONLY on
      the cap glyph, never as text. Reduced motion renders the meter as Text
      (no Progress fill at all). kit:v1 blocks only (Box, Text, Table,
      Progress). model.mjs is a pure reducer + render (MAX_SESSIONS 256,
      MAX_DIMENSIONS 32, every number re-clamped by count(), unknown kinds
      ignored); index.mjs is the #workshop-mod stdio loop verbatim but for
      the two views (no SDK import, echoes MOD_ABI_ID). State comes ONLY from
      the #mod-host feed projection v2 (numbers only, granted by log.read);
      a relayed render never replays fixtureEvents. requires log.read,
      egress none, no tools or commands. Fixtures strip, strip-reduced,
      over-budget, breaker, compacted with golden renders
      (test/ledger-mod.test.ts, light and dark); goldens regenerate with
      `npm run repin:first-party` in packages/gnomon.
    tags: [mods, first-party]
